USR0000038	DST0000069	5	Ho Chi Minh City People's Committee serves as the executive body of Vietnam's largest metropolis.Housed in the historic City Hall building built during the French colonial period (19021908), it reflects the layered history of the city once known as Saigon. After 1975, the building became the seat of the municipal government, symbolizing political transformation and national reunification. Architecturally, its elegant facade, arched windows, and clock tower showcase French colonial design adapted to a tropical setting. Beyond the facade, the illuminated building with Nguyen Hue Walking Street has become a civic landmark and gathering space, embodying both historical memory and modern urban vitality.Ho Chi Minh City People's Committee is the largest municipal executive organ in Vietnam, along with its political office building, the Ho Chi Minh City, the official administrative center of the country, and the historical center of the colonial period, the cultural center of the city.	2026-04-09 15:47:17.788+00	2026-04-09 15:47:17.788+00
